      "answer": "**Three-Part Study Guide: Pump Operation Procedure**\n=====================================================\n\n### Part 1: Inspection\n\nBefore starting the pump, inspect the inlet for debris and check that the pressure gauge reads zero.\n\n**Practice Question:** What is the first step to take before starting the pump?\n\n### Part 2: Operation\n\n1. Open the inlet valve before starting the pump.\n2. Stop the pump if pressure exceeds 90 kPa.\n\n**Practice Question:** What is the maximum pressure allowed before stopping the pump?\n\n### Part 3: Shutdown\n\n1. Turn the motor off.\n2. Close the inlet valve.\n3. Record the final pressure.\n4. Do not open the casing while the pump is pressurized.\n\n**Practice Question:** What should not be done while the pump is pressurized?\n\n### Short Answer Key\n\n1. What is the purpose of inspecting the inlet before starting the pump?\nAnswer: To ensure the inlet is clear of debris and the pressure gauge reads zero.\n2. What is the maximum pressure allowed before stopping the pump?\nAnswer: 90 kPa.\n3. What should not be done while the pump is pressurized?\nAnswer: Open the casing.\n\n> Coverage check: 3 of 3 source sections have no linked substantive passage in this answer. The response may be incomplete; full coverage is not verified.",
